 and it presumably based  on the laws of supply and demand should  reduce gas prices at least to some  degree number two do a gas tax holiday  gas tax holiday will temporarily uh  lower the price of gas and people can  stock up on gas if they want if there's  no limit on how much you can buy and  number three is tap into the strategic  petroleum reserve strategic petroleum  reserve  can um  depending on who you ask lower gas  prices temporarily between 12 and 18  cents per gallon some people say up to  25  slightly different numbers depending on  who you ask those are the things the  president can do but if you're fox news  and you've been playing the gas prices  up is all thanks to biden to some degree  don't you have to give them credit  credit for prices going down and just  imagine the fox news editorial meeting  okay  we can't talk about rising gas prices  anymore any other ideas how about this  let's slam that they're coming down too  quickly  that it will hurt gas stations  and that joe biden is being  braggadocious about it  that's what they did that's what they're  doing when fox news starts complaining  that the gas prices are falling too  quickly you start to know something's  wrong and uh it wouldn't surprise me to  see a headline like  did joe biden lower gas prices  to distract  from hunter biden's laptop i haven't  seen that  that's imaginary  but it wouldn't surprise me what we did  see and i'm not joking by the way about  the gas stations thing we looked at this  last week here's fox news bemoaning  lower gas prices because mom and pop gas  stations could be hurt i  want him to run again  and the rest probably don't that is  stunning by the way on gas prices i  found it curious i was at a lacrosse  tournament up in wilmington delaware  over the weekend in delaware and  northern maryland regular gas is about  anywhere from 455 to 480 a gallon so the  price is beginning to creep back down it  is it is and the point was made over the  weekend i believe it's a wall street  journal that gas prices are actually  coming back down historically faster  with the price of oil than usual oh they  might be coming down too quickly this  goes to show you what an incredible risk  reward calculation has to happen on the  part of those small independently owned  most of them mom and pop gas stations  it's a struggle for all of them now  that's not really true and there's a  bunch of different things that go into  that just to quickly refresh your memory  without going back into it  first  gas stations make very little off of  selling gas that's number one and number  two  their margin is very similar whether gas  prices are high or low right i mean if  your markup is on average seven to ten  cents per gallon if you sell it for five  bucks a gallon you make seven to ten  cents per gallon and if you sell it for  two bucks a gallon you make seven to ten  cents per gallon  sometimes high gas prices are actually  bad for gas stations when gas prices are  really high  you will sometimes see gas stations eat  a little bit of the cost  they will accept if everybody's  accepting a seven cent profit you might  see a gas station go you know what we  make more from the slurpees and the ring  dings and the honey buns and the entire  thing  so  we're going to just eat some of this  price increase to be the cheapest in the  area we'll just accept like a two cent  profit on gas or maybe just no profit to  get people in buying the higher uh  higher margin stuff so not only are  higher gas prices not necessarily good  for local gas stations sometimes they're  actually bad but fox news won't tell you  that they'll just say oh no what is joe  biden irresponsible for so quickly  lowering gas prices but it's also  nothing that he did but if he did it  then it's bad give me a break guys we'll  have this clip on our instagram you can  find us on instagram at david pakman  show see you there  if you're using traditional toilet paper  and paper towels y